---
import { SITE, CONTACT } from '~/consts';
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '~/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import type { Crumb } from '~/types';

const crumbs: Crumb[] = [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Privacy' }];
const updated = 'September 24, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What FindTool collects, what it does not, and why the content you paste into a tool never leaves your browser."
  canonical="/privacy"
>
  <div class="py-6 sm:py-8">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="bc-prose mt-6">
      <h2>The short version</h2>
      <p>
        FindTool does not collect the content you paste into its tools, does not require an
        account, and does not set advertising or tracking cookies. We collect aggregate,
        anonymous traffic statistics so we know which tools are worth improving.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong
          >We never collect, transmit, log or store the data you enter into a FindTool tool.</strong
        >
        The JSON you format, the token you decode, the password you generate, the file you hash and
        the text you diff are processed by JavaScript running in your own browser. That content is
        never sent to us, because the site has no server-side component that could receive it.
      </p>
      <p>
        This is a property of how the site is built, not a policy we could quietly change. You can
        confirm it by opening your browser's developer tools, switching to the Network tab, and
        using any tool on the site.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do collect</h2>
      <p>
        We use <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics</strong>, a privacy-focused analytics service that
        does not use cookies, does not fingerprint visitors, and does not track people across
        sites. It records, in aggregate:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>which pages were visited, and how many times</li>
        <li>the referring site or search engine, where the browser provides one</li>
        <li>country, derived from IP address at the edge — the IP itself is not stored by us</li>
        <li>device type, browser and operating system</li>
        <li>page load performance measurements</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may also record anonymous interaction counts, such as "the copy button on the JSON
        Formatter was clicked". These counts contain the name of the action and the tool only.
        <strong>They never include any part of your input.</strong>
      </p>
      <p>
        None of this identifies you, and none of it is sold, rented or shared with advertisers or
        data brokers.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
      <p>
        FindTool sets no cookies — not for analytics, not for anything. It uses your browser's
        <code>localStorage</code> for three things, all of them conveniences:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>whether you chose light or dark mode</li>
        <li>
          the names of the last few tools you opened, so the homepage can offer them back. This
          is a list of tool names and nothing else — no timestamps, no identifiers, and nothing
          about what you did with them
        </li>
        <li>option settings on individual tools, such as your preferred indent width</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        All three stay on your device, are never transmitted, and are removed when you clear your
        browser data. None of them can identify you, and the site works normally if your browser
        blocks storage entirely.
      </p>

      <h2>Hosting and data processors</h2>
      <p>
        The site is hosted on <strong>Cloudflare Pages</strong> and served through Cloudflare's
        CDN. As with any website, Cloudflare processes technical connection data — including your
        IP address — in order to deliver pages and protect against attacks. This is handled under
        Cloudflare's own privacy terms. We do not have access to raw server logs containing
        individual IP addresses.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fonts are served from our own domain rather than a third-party font CDN, so no font
        provider receives a request from your browser.
      </p>

      <h2>Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        FindTool currently shows <strong>no advertising</strong> and includes no advertising
        scripts. If advertising is introduced in future — most likely Google AdSense — this policy
        will be updated before any ad code is deployed, and the update will state plainly what the
        ad provider collects and how to opt out. Advertising would never be given access to the
        content you enter into a tool.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Because we do not collect personal data, we generally hold nothing about you to access,
        correct or delete. If you have sent us an email, we hold that email. You can ask us to
        delete it at any time by writing to
        <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.privacy}`}>{CONTACT.privacy}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are in the EU, UK, or a US state with comparable legislation, the aggregate
        analytics described above are collected on the basis of legitimate interest in
        understanding site usage. No consent banner is shown because no consent-requiring
        technology is used.
      </p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        FindTool is a developer utility aimed at a professional audience. It is not directed at
        children and we do not knowingly collect information from anyone.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes materially — in particular, if advertising or any new third-party
        service is added — the "last updated" date above will change and the affected sections
        will be rewritten to describe the new behaviour accurately.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Privacy questions go to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.privacy}`}>{CONTACT.privacy}</a>.
        General enquiries go to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.general}`}>{CONTACT.general}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
